<h2>8. Using the Ollagraph Table Extraction API</h2>
<p>The Ollagraph /v1/extract/tables endpoint handles the parsing step. It takes an HTML string (<code>html</code>, required) plus optional <code>min_rows</code> and <code>min_columns</code> filters, and returns every &lt;table&gt; it finds. It does not fetch pages, so get the HTML first — with /v1/scrape (<code>"format": "html"</code>) or your own HTTP client — and pass it in.</p>
<pre><code># 1. Fetch the page's HTML (/v1/extract/tables does not fetch pages itself)
